<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tarcondimotus II Philopator</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 17 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tarcondimotus II Philopator was king of the Tarcondimotid realm in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a> in the late 1st century BCE and early 1st century CE. Son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarcondimotus-i">Tarcondimotus I</a>, who died fighting for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> in 31 BCE, he was deprived of his kingdom by Octavian but restored by Augustus in 20 BCE. After his death in 17 CE the kingdom came under Roman provincial rule.</p></div>
